{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And now come, curse for me, etc.</b> But Balaam said to HaShem, blessed be He, that Balak sent him 'Come, stab (קָבָה) for me.' And what Rashi explained — that 'קָבָה' is harsher than 'אָרָה,' and Balaam added of his own accord out of his hatred for Israel, and likewise 'וְגֵרַשְׁתִּיו' is harsher than 'וַאֲגָרְשֶׁנּוּ מִן הָאָרֶץ' — this is not sufficient. For did Balaam not know that their El loves Israel, and that through this addition he would diminish? For perhaps they would not grant him permission at all. And regarding Balak there is a difficulty: how could he be so ignorant? For at first he said 'Come, curse (אָרָה) for me,' and he was not granted, as it says: 'כִּי מֵאֵן ה׳ לְתִתִּי לַהֲלֹךְ עִמָּכֶם,' and afterward he asked 'Come, stab (קָבָה) for me' — is it conceivable that one to whom they refuse to give even a small thing goes back and asks for a great thing?" "Rather, it is certain that 'אָרָה' is harsher than 'קָבָה,' and the expression 'נַכֶּה' is harsher than the expression 'לְהִלָּחֵם,' and the expression 'וַאֲגָרְשֶׁנּוּ מִן הָאָרֶץ' is harsher than 'וְגֵרַשְׁתִּיו.' For the expression 'קָבָה' is not an expression of cursing, as it says (Genesis 30:28): 'נָקְבָה עָלַי שְׂכָרֶךָ' — rather, it means designating and specifying, or making a small hole in them, from the expression 'וַיִּקֹּב חֹר בְּדַלְתּוֹ' (II Kings 12:10). But 'אָרָה' is harsh, for in it there is cursing, in it there is excommunication. (Shevuot 36a) And likewise 'לְהִלָּחֵם' is not so decidedly evil, for one may wage war in order to save oneself alone; but 'נַכֶּה' means actually striking. And likewise 'וְגֵרַשְׁתִּיו' connotes driving him away only from upon himself alone; but 'וַאֲגָרְשֶׁנּוּ מִן הָאָרֶץ' connotes from the whole world. And with this everything is resolved: for Balak did not know that their El loves them so much; therefore he opened his mouth without limit and asked 'Curse (אָרָה) for me this people; perhaps I will be able to strike (נַכֶּה) them, and I will drive them out (וַאֲגָרְשֶׁנּוּ) from the land' — that is, utter destruction, I will drive all of them from the world. But Balaam knew that their El loves them, and it is obvious that from Heaven they would restrain him, and neither this nor that would succeed in his hand; therefore he said before the Holy One, blessed be He, that Balak asks only to repel them from upon himself — for if they come to wage war against him, they will pass through the territory of Moab without opposition, and it is just that some curse should take effect, to pierce a hole in his door, to diminish them a little. Therefore he said that Balak sent to him 'Stab (קָבָה) for me; perhaps I will be able to wage war (לְהִלָּחֵם) against him; and I will drive him out (וְגֵרַשְׁתִּיו).'" "And the Holy One, blessed be He, answered him: 'You shall not curse (תָאֹר) the people, for they are blessed (בָרוּךְ)' — that is to say, they are so blessed and blessing cleaves to them so firmly that there is no room for even the great cursing (אֲרִירָה) to take effect, and all the more so the small stabbing (קָבָה), which has no power to take effect against the force of the blessings. And when Balak saw that he was not granted the great request, and that from Heaven they restrained him from going with him, he returned to the small one and said: at the very least, come, stab (קָבָה) for me — for he did not know what HaShem had said to Balaam, 'for they are blessed (כִּי בָרוּךְ הוּא),' for Balaam did not tell his messengers anything except 'כִּי מֵאֵן ה׳ לְתִתִּי לַהֲלֹךְ עִמָּכֶם.' And he thought that perhaps they restrained him because I asked too harshly; therefore he asked the small one. And Balaam answered him: 'If Balak were to give me the fullness of his house, silver and gold, I cannot transgress the word of HaShem my Elohim, to do small or great' — not the small קָבָה and not the great אָרָה. And he should have put great before small, in the manner of 'not only this but even that' — rather, precisely to make a point from this: because I cannot do it — behold, if the matter were in my power, I would do not only the small but even the great. And thereby he revealed that all the schemes of his heart were toward evil." "And this is the interpretation of the verse 'And now come,' etc. With the word 'and now (וְעַתָּה)' he wanted to test him whether he had the power to curse at any time he wished — for if he would put him off and say, 'I need to wait until the hour when the Holy One, blessed be He, is angry,' there is no substance to it, for perhaps He will not be angry all these days; and as it is written: 'מָה אֶזְעֹם לֹא זָעַם ה׳.' Therefore he said 'Curse (אָרָה) for me' — according to my will, at the time I choose; or 'curse them' so that they will be 'for me (לִי)' — delivered into my hand; or 'for me (לִי)' — that no person would know the matter except I alone. 'Perhaps I will be able' — that the world will think that I am able, but in truth 'we will strike (נַכֶּה) him,' the two of us, I and you; and after the striking, 'I will drive him out (אֲגָרְשֶׁנּוּ)' — I alone. And he used the expression 'perhaps (אוּלַי)' about himself: for I am in doubt whether I will be able, but you are certain that together we will certainly strike; therefore he did not say 'perhaps we will be able to strike him.' 'For I know that whom you bless is blessed (מְבֹרָךְ)' — he did not say 'will be blessed (יְבֹרָךְ)' in the manner he said 'is cursed (יוּאָר),' because he told him: precisely in curses you have power, but not in blessings; for 'whom you bless' is already blessed — and you see this from his דרך אומנות, and you bless him in order to hang it on you; for if not so, when you aided Sihon, you would have cursed Moab — and why did you not bless Sihon? Rather, it is certain that you have no power in blessings, but only in curses, to swallow and to destroy — as the meaning of the name Balaam (בִּלְעָם) indicates. Therefore I ask of you a curse and not a blessing, that you bless me."], :book :numbers, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:42:51.650073050Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}